\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Training dynamics} across three architecturally distinct backbones (diffusion, flow matching, autoregressive). \textbf  {Top row:} understanding signals --- \emph  {proposer reward} (quality of self-generated questions), \emph  {SC entropy} (self-consistency disagreement among $N{=}7$ prompt perturbations), and \emph  {STE difficulty} (Solver Token Entropy, a token-level difficulty proxy). Proposer reward and SC entropy increase as the Proposer learns to generate harder, more informative questions. STE difficulty remains approximately stable throughout training, confirming it serves as a stationary reference signal rather than a drifting curriculum target. \textbf  {Bottom row:} generation signals --- \emph  {total reward} (weighted combination of generation assessment signals), \emph  {QA fidelity} (attribute-level accuracy via Solver re-verification), and \emph  {cycle consistency} (caption$\to $image$\to $caption round-trip coherence). Generation improvement is delayed relative to understanding as the generation loop requires warm-up before producing useful training signal. All three backbones show qualitatively similar trends, supporting the model-agnostic design.}}{12}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:training_dynamics}{{2}{12}{\textbf {Training dynamics} across three architecturally distinct backbones (diffusion, flow matching, autoregressive). \textbf {Top row:} understanding signals --- \emph {proposer reward} (quality of self-generated questions), \emph {SC entropy} (self-consistency disagreement among $N{=}7$ prompt perturbations), and \emph {STE difficulty} (Solver Token Entropy, a token-level difficulty proxy). Proposer reward and SC entropy increase as the Proposer learns to generate harder, more informative questions. STE difficulty remains approximately stable throughout training, confirming it serves as a stationary reference signal rather than a drifting curriculum target. \textbf {Bottom row:} generation signals --- \emph {total reward} (weighted combination of generation assessment signals), \emph {QA fidelity} (attribute-level accuracy via Solver re-verification), and \emph {cycle consistency} (caption$\to $image$\to $caption round-trip coherence). Generation improvement is delayed relative to understanding as the generation loop requires warm-up before producing useful training signal. All three backbones show qualitatively similar trends, supporting the model-agnostic design}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:training_dynamics@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][11][]12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {4.4}Ablation Study}{12}{subsection.4.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:ablation}{{4.4}{12}{Ablation Study}{subsection.4.4}{}}
\newlabel{sec:ablation@cref}{{[subsection][4][4]4.4}{[1][12][]12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Ablation study on BLIP3o-8B measuring the contribution of individual framework components. Each row removes or replaces one component while keeping all others at their default configuration.}}{12}{table.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{3}{12}{Ablation study on BLIP3o-8B measuring the contribution of individual framework components. Each row removes or replaces one component while keeping all others at their default configuration}{table.caption.19}{}}
\newlabel{tab:ablation@cref}{{[table][3][]3}{[1][12][]12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Signal analysis} on BLIP3o-8B. (a)~\emph  {STE curriculum progression:} the distribution of Solver Token Entropy difficulty shifts gradually rightward over training, indicating that the Proposer learns to generate progressively harder questions as the Solver improves. (b)~\emph  {Complementary difficulty dimensions:} STE and self-consistency (SC) entropy capture orthogonal aspects of question difficulty. Four quadrants emerge --- \emph  {token-hard} (high STE, low SC): questions with difficult tokens but consistent solver answers; \emph  {informative} (high both): boundary-level questions that maximise learning signal; \emph  {trivial} (low both): easy questions filtered out by the curriculum; \emph  {framing-hard} (low STE, high SC): questions where prompt framing causes solver disagreement. Dashed lines mark medians. (c)~\emph  {Generation reward components:} QA fidelity (attribute-level accuracy) and cycle consistency (holistic coherence) both improve, with fidelity rising faster. Generation signals are delayed relative to understanding due to the warm-up phase needed for stable generation rollouts.}}{13}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:signal_analysis}{{3}{13}{\textbf {Signal analysis} on BLIP3o-8B. (a)~\emph {STE curriculum progression:} the distribution of Solver Token Entropy difficulty shifts gradually rightward over training, indicating that the Proposer learns to generate progressively harder questions as the Solver improves. (b)~\emph {Complementary difficulty dimensions:} STE and self-consistency (SC) entropy capture orthogonal aspects of question difficulty. Four quadrants emerge --- \emph {token-hard} (high STE, low SC): questions with difficult tokens but consistent solver answers; \emph {informative} (high both): boundary-level questions that maximise learning signal; \emph {trivial} (low both): easy questions filtered out by the curriculum; \emph {framing-hard} (low STE, high SC): questions where prompt framing causes solver disagreement. Dashed lines mark medians. (c)~\emph {Generation reward components:} QA fidelity (attribute-level accuracy) and cycle consistency (holistic coherence) both improve, with fidelity rising faster. Generation signals are delayed relative to understanding due to the warm-up phase needed for stable generation rollouts}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig:signal_analysis@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][11][]13}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Qualitative analysis. \textbf  {Top:} self-consistency correction in understanding. \textbf  {Bottom:} QA-fidelity error detection in generation (BAGEL). Green indicates pass; red indicates fail.}}{14}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
